  "versionIdentifier": "2008",
  "versionSpecification": "The 2008 version provides an enhanced anatomical phantom based on averages of 27 T1-weighted, 11 T2-weighted, and 12 proton density-weighted MRI volumes (Aubert-Broche et al., 2006). The volumes are defined in Talairach stereotaxic space and represented on a 0.5 mm isotropic voxel grid. The anatomical phantom incorporates refined tissue segmentation and classification, using additional computed tomography (CT) and magnetic resonance angiography (MRA) information to improve the representation of brain and surrounding head tissues, particularly the skull and blood vessels. The distributed dataset includes averaged T1-weighted, T2-weighted, and PD-weighted volumes, a discrete tissue classification volume, and 12 probabilistic (fuzzy) tissue maps describing the fractional composition of different tissues within individual voxels. The discrete classification distinguishes cerebrospinal fluid, gray matter, white matter, fat, muscle, skin and muscle, skull, dura mater, bone marrow, and blood vessels."
